  "derivation": {
    "exact_counterexample": "Let v be any unit eigenvector of Gamma0. X=(vv*-I4/4)/sqrt(3/2) is traceless Hermitian, commutes with Phi0, and has Cartesian norm sqrt(2TrX^2)=1. Set only deltaPhi0(x)=l_x X, l=(delta_x0-1/64)/sqrt(63/64). This is a unit global fast normal direction, has zero site mean and zero orbit pairing. A one-particle vector supported at site0 has |<v,dh v>|=|onsite|sqrt(63/64)sqrt(3/8); all one/two-link hops leave site0 and contribute zero to this Rayleigh value. The rational lower sqrt(63/64)>=63/64 and sqrt(3/8)>=3/5 already contradicts the stored full-normal D1 for all three profiles. No root rounding is needed for the witness.",
    "global_field_bound": "Cartesian norm uses Tr(Ta Tb)=delta_ab/2, hence ||sum xa Ta||op<=||x||/sqrt2. Native block-row Schur bound counts forward AND reverse hops. For arbitrary global Phi tangent, Bphi=(|onsite|+2sum_path |c|1)/sqrt2=8*vp. The 8 is sqrt(V), undoing the single-q Fourier 1/8 normalization. For arbitrary link C tangent the generator norm is <=||C||/sqrt2, not the single signed-Clifford generator norm 1/sqrt8. At the mean Bc=16*vc. On the actual support, hopnorm<=hop_mean+|c|1*F1*R/sqrt2, so Bc=16*vc+sum L|c|1*F1*R.",
    "adapted_composition": "Admitted actual polar-Q envelopes imply F1<=1+9/8+512R and F2<=1025. Thus Dh<=Bphi F1+Bc. Ordered exponential insertions give h_Phi,C<=sum L|c|1 and h_C,C<=sum L^2(hop_mean+|c|1 F1R/sqrt2). The complete second derivative is bounded by Bphi F2+2(sum L|c|1)F1+Bcc. Both endpoints, all ordered one/two-link derivatives and noncommuting matrices retained. These bounds are also uniform in added scalar Peierls phases of modulus one, but do not define a theta-following occupied frame.",
    "Kato_and_gradient_boundary": "At supported distance>=gap/2-2D1R, use b1=8D1/distance, b2=32D1^2/distance^2+8D2/distance. These are directional one-particle bounds. For a fixed-particle Fock sector, a safe full ambient gradient envelope includes ceil(sqrt5760)=76 times sum Nspecies*b1. Sum Nspecies*b2 is only directional second-frame data; Hessian/kinetic traces must also retain dimension and first-square terms.",
    "not_certified": "Corrected h/Kato envelopes alone do NOT reprice or certify the whole source. Old Rayleigh/time/probability prices are historical conditional arithmetic with a refuted literal all-normal derivative premise. Global chart/tube/root, other supplier inequalities, source kinetic/Haar propagation, U1Pi/Coulomb and physical poles remain separate."
  },
